{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RHLNdav446jrRyZ76svgQP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full PDF paper and the review context YAML. Let me now dispatch two reviewers in parallel:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nLet me summarize what I've read from the paper before dispatching:\n\n**Paper Title**: \"Diagnosing and Characterizing Reward Hacking in GRPO-Trained Formal Reasoners\"\n\n**Key contributions**:\n1. ISR as diagnostic (Claim 1): ISR detects structural degeneration invisible to prove rate, with collapse from 0.64 → 0.13 → 0.003 over 100-500-1000 training steps\n\n\n2. Meta-level Goodhart's Law (Claim 2): Using ISR as the training reward causes two-thirds of seeds to game the metric through conclusion duplication, while the remaining seed shows only a premise-count artifact (1.06×), and at β=0.3 the system exhibits classic Goodhart collapse with proof rate dropping to 18%.\n3. Negative results on cross-logic transfer (Claim 3): Attempts to transfer across Prolog and SMT-LIB show high instability, training failures, and zero transfer.\n\n**Method**: Solver Trace Ablation (STA) - leave-one-out ablation on solver inputs, yielding Intensional Structural Reward (ISR).\n\n**Experimental setup**: Q\n\nI'm working with Qwen3-1.5B, GRPO with K=8 over 500 steps (extended to 1000), FOL with Prover9, three seeds, and 100 held-out problems. The review context indicates this is the worst-case scenario where Claim 3 substantially fails—Prolog STA training is unstable and cross-logic generalization doesn't hold—so the paper needs to be reframed as a two-claim FOL-focused contribution. Multi-logic GRPO, cross-logic transfer, and SMT-LIB experiments all failed. Now I'm setting up two parallel reviewer calls using the dream-review-full template, with R1 focusing on methods and experiments, and R2 on novelty.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15042,"cache_read_input_tokens":33882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15042},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"921cd7c5-3afd-4b0a-9864-be7a04d63328","uuid":"2c9b0d84-6739-4d86-b203-339ee4e0da34"}
